# KraftMart

> KraftMart (https://kraftmart.shop) is an Indian e-commerce store based in Amritsar, Punjab, that sells handcrafted Indian wedding swords, Rajput talwars, Punjabi khandas, Damascus steel swords, Sikh religious articles, and decorative handforged items, with worldwide shipping and cash-on-delivery for India.

KraftMart is operated by Lakshmi Engineering Works, a metal-craft business founded in 1996 in Amritsar, Punjab that originally specialized in nickel and chrome electroplating, polishing, and job-work manufacturing of machinery parts, hand-tool drilling machines, vintage-vehicle accessories, and kirpan/sword blades. Building on this manufacturing background and its ties to the local Sikh community, the company launched its own product line, KraftMart, on 1 November 2019, moving from marketplaces such as Etsy, eBay, and Instagram to its own Shopify store. KraftMart sells handcrafted, made-to-order and ready-made swords and related handicrafts, primarily for Indian wedding (baraat/dulha) ceremonies, Sikh religious use, and home decor or collectible display. Products include wedding and groom swords (talwars, tegas/teghs), Punjabi khandas, Damascus steel swords, Maratha-style Bhavani talwars, Sikh kirpans and religious articles (including Prakash Teer, Chakar, and Chaur for Guru Granth Sahib prakash), collectible swords (e.g. replica cavalry swords), daggers, wall hangings, miniature collectibles, and silver calligraphy pieces. Many products offer free custom engraving and personalization. KraftMart ships worldwide via India Post International, FedEx, and DHL, and domestically within India via Delhivery, DTDC, and India Post, with cash-on-delivery available for Indian customers (15% advance booking plus 85% cash on delivery, or a discount for full advance payment). The primary content language is English; the storefront interface also offers French, Arabic, and Simplified Chinese, and supports checkout in multiple regional currencies displayed in INR.

